  "generated_text": "1. First, we need to determine the total number of jelly beans in the bag.\n2. The bag contains 5 red, 6 green, 7 yellow, and 8 blue jelly beans.\n3. Adding these together, we get:\n   \\[\n   5 + 6 + 7 + 8 = 26\n   \\]\n   So, there are 26 jelly beans in total.\n\n4. Next, we need to find the probability of selecting a blue jelly bean.\n5. There are 8 blue jelly beans in the bag.\n6. The probability \\( P \\) of selecting a blue jelly bean is given by the ratio of the number of blue jelly beans to the total number of jelly beans:\n   \\[\n   P(\\text{blue}) = \\frac{\\text{Number of blue jelly beans}}{\\text{Total number of jelly beans}} = \\frac{8}{26}\n   \\]\n\n7. Simplify the fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{8}{26} = \\frac{4}{13}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability is \\boxed{\\frac{4}{13}}.",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[4/13, '\\\\frac{4}{13}']",
    "gold_answer": "In total, there are $5+6+7+8=26$ jelly beans in the bag.\n\nSince there are 8 blue jelly beans, the probability of selecting a blue jelly bean is  $$\\frac{8}{26}=\\boxed{\\frac{4}{13}}.$$",
